--- body ---
## Context

All existing RAG ablation data (Phase 1: 118 runs, Phase 2: deleted)
was collected with temperature=null (uncontrolled) and, for some Phase 2
runs, with OpenRouter web_search injecting ~300K tokens of search results.

PR #257 landed the fix: JobSpec.web_search defaults to false, 16 Phase 2
sweep configs added to experiments.toml. The code path through worker.py
now respects the sweep config.

## Actions

1. Re-run Phase 2 RAG sweeps (16 configs × 2 models × 2 reps = 64 calls).
   Use the `ablation_p2_rag_*` sweep configs in experiments.toml.
2. Assess Phase 1 RAG data (118 runs, all t=null). Decide whether to
   re-run at t=0 or document the limitation.
3. Rebuild measurements.jsonl after each batch.
4. Verify: all new runs have temperature=0.0, token counts ~72K
   (no 300K+ outliers from web search injection).

## Test

`grep -c '"temperature":0.0' measurements.jsonl` matches new run count.
No `"temperature":null` entries in new ablation data.

## Exit criteria

- Phase 2: 64 clean measurements from sweep configs, no manual runs
- Phase 1: re-run or documented limitation
- ΔF1 per module computable without confounds
